WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.339
This is not a dog.

00:00:01.339 --> 00:00:02.399
You heard me right.

00:00:02.399 --> 00:00:04.980
Blue from Blue's Clues is not a dog.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.670
Sure, she looks like a dog and she barks like
a dog.

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:09.610
But she is not a dog.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:13.880
Get this, Blue is in fact an advanced member
of an alien species looking to learn from

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:18.869
humans in an eventual bid to take over planet
Earth, an alien species that is getting closer

00:00:18.869 --> 00:00:21.650
to achieving that goal season by season.

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.720
And here's the craziest part, this is barely
a theory.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.681
As you're about to see, practically all of
this is explicitly spelled out in the show's canon.

00:00:29.681 --> 00:00:34.500
So sit down in your thinking chair and Think,
Think, Think.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.600
about your impending servitude to an army
of canine themed overlords.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.359
*Blue barks*
That's alien for sit and obey.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.710
Hello Internet!

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:49.480
Welcome to Film Theory, the show that's really
found its niche talking about the dark lore

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:51.960
of children's programming starring puppies.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:55.789
It is a very specific content category, but
we are dialed into it.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:59.530
For those of you who have no idea what's going
on today we're talking about Blue's Clues,

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:04.809
the iconic Nickelodeon kids show that ran
for ten years between 1996 and 2006 before

00:01:04.809 --> 00:01:07.070
getting revived in 2019.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:10.680
Every episode was an interactive audience
adventure as the animated dog Blue and her

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:15.040
human companion roamed around their storybook
house in order to find three clues that would

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.170
help them solve the episode's big mystery.

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:20.970
Honestly, when you look at it, this thing
was like the training ground for theorists

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:22.040
of the future.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.610
Blue's Clues walked so Film Theory could run.

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:28.106
Along the way, they'd sing songs, read the
mail, and do stuff like this.

00:01:34.572 --> 00:01:38.479
You know, the good sort of formulaic that
any kid's show really thrives off of.

00:01:38.479 --> 00:01:41.780
The show was hosted by Steve for Four Seasons,
who then went off to college and pass the

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:43.960
baton over to his younger brother, Joe.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.610
Now, in its current iteration, Blue's Clues
&amp; You!

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:51.290
It's hosted by their cousin Josh, all wearing
primary colors, all equally oblivious to the

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:54.295
obvious answers that are lying right in front
of their faces.

00:02:00.864 --> 00:02:01.651
Sure, Steve.

00:02:01.651 --> 00:02:03.820
I’m sure your dog Blue wants to eat a bubble
sandwich.

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:04.820
Try it.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:07.510
See how much dog vomit you're cleaning up
out of that carpet.

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:12.040
Anyway, Blue's Clues is probably, in my opinion,
one of the best kid's programs of all time.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:13.490
If you've never seen it.

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:15.000
Who taught you how to feel?

00:02:22.986 --> 00:02:23.830
Me too, Steve.

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:25.120
I didn't forget you either.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:26.900
Who is cutting onions in here?

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:30.800
Anyway, now that my family's exhausted the
entire canon of Paw Patrol and is currently

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:33.380
waiting patiently for the new movie to release
later this year.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:37.230
We've moved on to revisiting some classic
Blue's Clues in order to fill the void in

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:38.690
our Friday night movie nights.

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:42.069
And let me tell you, let's go back to the
show as an adult I’m picking up on a lot

00:02:42.069 --> 00:02:46.519
of small, strange details here and there,
things that seriously make me use my mind

00:02:46.519 --> 00:02:47.980
and take a step at a time.

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:51.530
And I got to tell you, it's time to do the
thing that I want to do, which is expose Blue's

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:54.340
Clues for the alien conspiracy that it is.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.870
You see, the colorful storybook world of Blue's
Clues holds a secret in its later seasons

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:03.519
and spin off movies, a secret that recontextualized
the entirety of the show.

00:03:03.519 --> 00:03:06.709
For decades, we've been led to believe that
Blue is a puppy.

00:03:06.709 --> 00:03:08.080
Nope, she is anything but.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.409
She is an emissary from the stars scouting
out us earthlings.

00:03:11.409 --> 00:03:13.510
And our reckoning is coming, friends.

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:15.830
So skidoo on over, because it's.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:23.756
(Beautiful singing voice): Theory Time, Theory
Time, Theory Time!

00:03:23.756 --> 00:03:24.714
(Slippery Ash): Ooh, a clue.

00:03:24.714 --> 00:03:25.525
A clue.

00:03:25.525 --> 00:03:26.310
Oh, what did you say?

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:27.850
You have the flu?

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:28.850
Sorry to hear that.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.510
I've been sick too, lately. You can probably
hear it in my voice.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.430
It's been a really nasty winter so far.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:34.510
(Slippery Ash): No, a clue.

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:35.819
Oh, you see a clue.

00:03:35.819 --> 00:03:36.890
Thanks, Slippery.

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:39.239
The first clue is the subscribe button.

00:03:39.239 --> 00:03:42.420
Let's put that in our handy dandy
(Slippery Ash) :Notebook!

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:43.420
Wacom tablet.

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:44.420
Right.

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:45.950
So we draw one long line at the top.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.349
A long line at the bottom.

00:03:47.349 --> 00:03:51.670
Connect the two with some rounded lines at
the ends, and then we write the word “Subscribed”

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:52.670
in the middle.

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:53.900
Wait, does yours not look like that?

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:54.900
You better fix that.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.500
Otherwise, Mailbox is going to cry.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:59.050
And you don't want to make Mailbox cry, do
you?

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:00.689
Let's begin in a simple place, shall we?

00:04:00.689 --> 00:04:01.689
Blue’s Age.

00:04:01.689 --> 00:04:05.060
The sheer fact that Blue is still alive in
the new reboot series automatically throws

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:10.500
her dog-ness into question, considering that
she should 100% be dead at this point.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:13.910
You see in the world of the show, there is
clearly a passage of time that's established.

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:17.530
For the most obvious example of this: In season
four, Steve goes off to college.

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:18.269
There. Done.

00:04:18.269 --> 00:04:21.320
Time is not a frozen entity inside this universe.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:25.080
Season five Episode 29 tells us the story
of how Steve first met Blue.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:28.571
At the time she was a young puppy and Steve
looked to be about eight years old, which

00:04:28.571 --> 00:04:33.180
tells us that they were together for at least
ten years before Joe entered the picture.

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:35.900
Now, in Season two Episode nine - Blue's Birthday.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:37.900
Blue's Cake has eight candles in it.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:39.169
And we're not talking dog years either.

00:04:39.169 --> 00:04:42.639
I think we've all heard the general rule of
thumb that one year for a dog equals about

00:04:42.639 --> 00:04:44.490
seven years of human life.

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:48.860
So if your dog is two real years old, it's
dog age would be about like 14, right?

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:51.910
Well, it turns out the math isn't exactly
that simple.

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:55.229
Dogs mature more quickly than we do early
on in their life.

00:04:55.229 --> 00:05:00.620
Size and breed also play a factor with smaller
dogs tending to live longer than larger ones.

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:03.550
So knowing that, what would Blue's age expectancy
be?

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:08.139
Well, based on her large floppy ears, she's
likely one of the breeds from the hound family.

00:05:08.139 --> 00:05:14.259
We also know that Blue talks a lot in yowling
barks and high pitched whines.

00:05:14.259 --> 00:05:18.800
This also fits with the hound group; as dogs
bred for hunting have a very similar, distinctive

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:22.449
sound and tend to be more talkative than other
dogs because they had to communicate with

00:05:22.449 --> 00:05:23.729
their humans while on the chase.

00:05:23.729 --> 00:05:26.400
But the thing that actually clinches it is
her weight.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:30.020
We know, based on Blue's visit to the vet
in season five, episode 30, that she weighs

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:31.650
in at…

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:34.100
Which would put her as one of the smaller
hounds.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:39.259
In other words, Blue most closely resembles
a beagle, giving her a rough life expectancy

00:05:39.259 --> 00:05:40.770
of 15 years.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.229
At absolute best.

00:05:42.229 --> 00:05:47.520
The record for the oldest dog in history is
22 years, and I doubt that they were as sprightly

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:49.050
as our puppy Blue here.

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:53.860
So if Blue was eight at the top of season
two and now 23 years later, we have this new

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:58.520
reboot, there is no way that she would still
be qualifying for puppy status, let alone

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:00.830
living status if she were actually a dog.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:01.830
What's that?

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:03.539
Maybe time froze between the season breaks.

00:06:03.539 --> 00:06:06.039
I mean, you would think that, but no.

00:06:06.039 --> 00:06:08.840
Time continued to march forward for all of
the characters.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:11.460
Case in point, Mr. Salt and Mrs. Pepper.

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:15.740
In the season one finale of Blue's Clues,
the big mystery solve is that these two seasonings

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:17.990
are having themselves a baby named Paprika.

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:19.199
It is really cute.

00:06:19.199 --> 00:06:22.210
By the fourth season, paprika has become a
toddler.

00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:24.300
Two years have passed in two seasons.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:27.759
In season four, the family has themselves
another child: Cinnamon.

00:06:27.759 --> 00:06:31.009
By the series wrap, Cinnamon is still a baby
that can barely talk.

00:06:31.009 --> 00:06:32.009
But hold on.

00:06:32.009 --> 00:06:34.669
In this new reboot series, Blue's Clues &amp; You!

00:06:34.669 --> 00:06:35.759
Everyone is older.

00:06:35.759 --> 00:06:40.069
Paprika is a teenager with a smartphone, and
Cinnamon is probably around ten, wearing a

00:06:40.069 --> 00:06:41.949
cool sideways ball cap.

00:06:41.949 --> 00:06:46.419
The full 21 year gap between the original
series finale and the reboot hasn't passed,

00:06:46.419 --> 00:06:51.259
but it has been at least a decade for the
characters inside of this world, meaning that

00:06:51.259 --> 00:06:54.710
Blue is likely 21 years old or older.

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:58.610
That is not a dog who is able to dance, party
and freeze on a single toe.

00:06:58.610 --> 00:07:02.110
And the lies and the deceit about Blue's age
don't stop there.

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:05.830
If you jump to the reboot and watch season
one Episode 11 - Happy Birthday Blue.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:07.229
Count the candles on the cake.

00:07:07.229 --> 00:07:11.050
Not only has she not aged, apparently she's
aged backwards.

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:16.120
Her cake only has five candles, three less
than what she had when it was her birthday

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:17.120
with Steve.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:18.650
The evidence here just doesn't add up.

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:22.120
And before you think that maybe this is a
new replacement dog, it's not.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:26.749
It is confirmed to be the same Blue from the
old series by both Steve and Joe.

00:07:38.129 --> 00:07:42.710
So if it's the same dog 20 plus years later,
how can Blue still be alive and kicking?

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:47.430
The only reasonable explanation is that Blue
isn't a dog at all.

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:49.449
But to prove that, we've got to find ourselves
some more clues.

00:07:49.449 --> 00:07:50.449
(Slippery Ash): A clue. A clue!

00:07:50.449 --> 00:07:51.449
Tattoo. Tattoo?

00:07:51.449 --> 00:07:51.949
Yeah.

00:07:51.949 --> 00:07:52.949
I got one on the small of my back.

00:07:52.949 --> 00:07:53.744
It's a cute little butterfly.

00:07:53.744 --> 00:07:54.302
Why do you ask?

00:07:54.302 --> 00:07:55.130
(Disappointed Ash): No, Matt.

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:55.891
A clue.

00:07:55.891 --> 00:07:58.003
Oh, a clue.

00:07:58.003 --> 00:07:58.883
And it's on Blue's Paw Prints.

00:07:58.883 --> 00:07:59.883
Isn't that meta?

00:07:59.883 --> 00:08:01.670
So why would Blue's Pop be a clue?

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:04.039
Well, it's because her anatomy isn't like
a dog.

00:08:04.039 --> 00:08:07.599
For starters, she's able to pick up books
with an opposable thumb.

00:08:07.599 --> 00:08:11.819
You don't have to be a vet or have a masters
in animal sciences to know that dogs do not

00:08:11.819 --> 00:08:12.819
have thumbs.

00:08:12.819 --> 00:08:16.450
And yet, on many occasions throughout the
show and the promotional artwork, we see blue

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:22.599
holding things, rowing rafts, holding a piping
bag or a guitar, all with a big ol’ prominent thumb.

00:08:22.599 --> 00:08:26.139
A thumb that is somehow able to retract back
into her hand.

00:08:26.139 --> 00:08:27.610
Sorry, let me rephrase this.

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:30.419
Blue's whole paw is able to morph and change.

00:08:30.419 --> 00:08:34.229
Blue normally has herself three obvious toes
as she hops around the house.

00:08:34.229 --> 00:08:37.930
This is consistent to her design across all
iterations of the show, and yet when she goes

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:42.580
up to smash a paw print on the screen for
a clue or during the intro sequence, she grows

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.120
a fourth toe.

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:48.550
And also, again, there's that humanoid monkey
thumb that's hidden somewhere in there, too.

00:08:48.550 --> 00:08:50.430
This is not normal dog anatomy.

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:53.030
Why has this not raised anyone's alarms before?

00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:55.240
And the non dog behavior doesn't stop there
either.

00:08:55.240 --> 00:09:00.010
In Season six Episode eight - Soccer Practice,
Blue and the gang play a game of soccer.

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:02.970
After they're done, they all sit down to share
some chocolate ice cream.

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:03.491
Yep.

00:09:03.491 --> 00:09:05.530
You heard that one right, chocolate ice cream.

00:09:05.530 --> 00:09:10.649
I think most people know that giving a dog
chocolate is basically like giving them poison.

00:09:10.649 --> 00:09:12.980
But ice cream is just as bad for the dog.

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:14.890
It can lead to bloating and vomiting.

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:19.000
But here at the end of the episode, both Blue
and her friend Magenta are eating chocolate

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:20.000
ice cream.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.310
Clearly, there are two impostors among us.

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:26.450
And right now, Blue and Magenta be looking
mad sus.

00:09:26.450 --> 00:09:29.250
Whatever she's doing, she is clearly not a
dog.

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:32.550
How, then, can I prove that she's from another
planet?

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:34.800
Well, just by watching the show.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:38.990
In season six episode one - The Legend of
the Blue Puppy, Joe and the gang are watching

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:39.990
a blue moon.

00:09:39.990 --> 00:09:42.733
All of a sudden, Moona the moon fairy appears.

00:09:48.446 --> 00:09:51.170
As the story goes on the night of the very
first blue moon.

00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:53.500
A whole litter of puppies just appeared out
of nowhere.

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:56.050
But one was different from all the others.

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:57.324
She was blue.

00:10:03.876 --> 00:10:05.329
That is not a dog.

00:10:05.329 --> 00:10:08.310
That is an alien trying to look like a dog
and failing miserably.

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:11.830
It's also at this point that I should probably
mention Blue's other origin story.

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:16.120
In Season Five's holiday episode, we find
out that Blue Again is no normal dog.

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:20.485
Instead, she appeared out of a storybook just
because Steve wished her into reality.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:32.269
Steve gets this mysterious book in the mail
from an unmarked package about a blue dog

00:10:32.269 --> 00:10:34.097
who doesn't do normal dog things.

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:45.190
We're told that Blue wants a friend who can
teach her all the songs and stories and games.

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:48.982
The book then ends with the most abrupt fourth
wall break imaginable.

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:56.880
That night, Blue jumps out of the book using
the magical power of skidooing, and the rest

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:57.880
is history.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:01.250
Now it would seem like the blue moon and book
stories would contradict, but they don't.

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:02.880
In fact, they just repeat each other.

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:05.180
They're just the same story being told differently.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:09.110
Blue is a creature that came into being because
of the blue moon and was immediately different

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:10.200
from normal dogs.

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:14.480
That much is very clear and it would seem
that one power that the moon puppies possess

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:19.010
is the power to skidoo, hopping into fictional
worlds like books and paintings.

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:22.860
This is a skill that seems specific to moon
puppies like Blue, who are then able to pass

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:26.580
along those abilities to their caretakers
who get exposed to her.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:30.480
Notice how shocked everyone is the first time
that she skidoos into a world, but eventually

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:31.799
they're all doing it.

00:11:58.026 --> 00:12:02.240
Anyway, Blue wound up inside of a book, waiting
for the right human caretaker who would then

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:04.110
be able to teach her human ways.

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:06.610
But skidooing isn't her only magic power.

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:09.860
Returning back to the moon fairies in the
Legend of the Blue Puppy episode, we see that

00:12:09.860 --> 00:12:12.214
blue has an even greater ability.

00:12:21.552 --> 00:12:23.012
Spoiler alert it's not what you expect.

00:12:32.342 --> 00:12:32.988
Yep.

00:12:32.988 --> 00:12:34.360
A mysterious key.

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:37.300
Late season Blue's Clues gets to some weird
places, man.

00:12:37.300 --> 00:12:42.250
The TL;DW of all this is That Blue is finally
old enough to unlock her secret ability.

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:46.094
The key, which has been hidden inside her
alien dog stuffed animal the whole time.

00:12:46.094 --> 00:12:47.162
Hint Hint.

00:12:47.162 --> 00:12:49.190
Opens Blue's magical playroom.

00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:53.037
Blue transforms into a giant puppets and she
can talk.

00:13:06.588 --> 00:13:08.320
No, no, no, thank you.

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:10.370
I'll just go back to the barking, please.

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:13.860
What's also interesting is that time moves
differently inside of Blue's room.

00:13:13.860 --> 00:13:17.449
We can actually see from the clock in the
background that each toy box segment here

00:13:17.449 --> 00:13:20.380
doesn't run as the same time outside of the
toy box.

00:13:20.380 --> 00:13:24.899
The whole thing functions a lot like the hyperbolic
time chamber from Dragon Ball Z, where decades

00:13:24.899 --> 00:13:28.730
of training can get done inside the room in
mere minutes of real time.

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:30.810
So is this a similar sort of facility?

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:34.199
Is Blue's Room a place for Blue to hone her
powers of human speech?

00:13:34.199 --> 00:13:36.480
Seems like the next clear evolution for Blue
species.

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:40.370
So if Blue were to harness her true alien
powers within Blue's room, what would the

00:13:40.370 --> 00:13:43.250
fully evolved form of Blue's species look
like?

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:47.650
Ladies and gentlemen, allow me to introduce
you to Rainbow Puppy, the newest addition

00:13:47.650 --> 00:13:50.230
to the roster added as a part of the reboot.

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:54.380
Rather than just being one color, Rainbow
Puppy is, as you might have guessed, a Rainbow.

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:55.620
RGB gamer for life.

00:13:55.620 --> 00:14:00.050
More importantly, though, she can speak fluent
English and walks on two feet rather than

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:01.680
four like Blue and Magenta.

00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:06.160
Not only does this make Rainbow Puppy less
doglike, she's clearly a more powerful version

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:07.160
of Blue.

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:11.230
In season three Episode 11 of the reboot - Rainbow
Puppies Skidoo Adventure, we see that she

00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:13.610
can skidoo way more than Blue ever could.

00:14:13.610 --> 00:14:17.430
In most episodes, Blue only manages to skidoo
like once, maybe twice.

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:21.959
But in this episode, Rainbow Puppy skidoos
into Chalk World, The Post Office, The Farm,

00:14:21.959 --> 00:14:25.750
the ocean, the Theater, Rainbow World and
finally Skidoo World.

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:31.330
Seven times in a single episode, she is clearly
far stronger than Blue or Magenta ever were.

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:33.130
And on top of that, she doesn't have an owner.

00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:36.500
Blue and Magenta both have owners, but I'm
guessing Rainbow Puppy doesn't because of

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:37.500
her abilities.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:42.010
She doesn't need a caretaker like the others
because she's a fully evolved version of…whatever

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:44.460
alien species these creatures are meant to
be.

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:45.560
Will the same happen to Blue?

00:14:45.560 --> 00:14:49.200
Will she soon have enough power of her own
that she no longer requires an owner?

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.200
Absolutely.

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:53.230
You can actually see the start of it once
Blue unlocks her room.

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:56.480
Joe, her caretaker at the time, is completely
sidelined.

00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:58.199
He doesn't know where Blue's disappeared off
to.

00:14:58.199 --> 00:15:01.311
Heck, he doesn't even learn about Blue's Room
until we tell him.

00:15:15.050 --> 00:15:16.946
He's clearly left on the outs.

00:15:25.350 --> 00:15:28.100
With Steve, it was always about his relationship
with Blue.

00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:31.709
But once Blue unlocks her final ability, Joe
serves no purpose.

00:15:31.709 --> 00:15:33.279
He's not needed anymore.

00:15:33.279 --> 00:15:37.800
It's all about you, the viewer, the one who's
allowed inside of Blue's Room.

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:41.870
In fact, Blue is so not interested in Joe
anymore that she doesn't even play Blue's

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:42.870
Clues with him.

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:45.551
Joe has to be the one to create the game himself.

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:52.420
We would not.

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:53.560
Joe is an afterthought.

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:55.380
The humans have served their purpose.

00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:59.540
We even catch glimpses of blue standing on
two feet in the recently released movie.

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:02.329
She's starting to evolve into a higher powered
being.

00:16:02.329 --> 00:16:05.089
She's starting to approach the levels of Rainbow
Puppy.

00:16:05.089 --> 00:16:09.079
In this new Blue's Clues movie, we see Blue's
powers to an extreme degree.

00:16:09.079 --> 00:16:12.550
She's able to skidoo a whole bus through a
billboard to get to New York City.

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:16.230
And while they're in New York, everyday items
like a mailbox, mustard and salt and pepper

00:16:16.230 --> 00:16:18.740
shakers come to life as Blue walks past.

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:21.680
Blue has the ability to create living beings.

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:24.680
So we've established that Blue is clearly
not a dog from Earth.

00:16:24.680 --> 00:16:26.040
But what's the goal here?

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:31.980
Well, after sitting down in my thinking chair
to think, think, think, I realize Blue's true

00:16:31.980 --> 00:16:32.980
purpose.

00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:34.970
She's training up to become the next Rainbow
Dog.

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:36.450
And so what's Rainbow Dog's deal?

00:16:36.450 --> 00:16:37.450
Domination.

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:40.910
In Rainbow Puppies Skidoo Adventure we see
Skidoo World for the first time ever.

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:43.600
The world that Josh and blue travel between
when they skidoo.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.810
In this world I noticed a few interesting
things.

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:48.800
One, it's rainbow colored, showing rainbow
control over this meta-space.

00:16:48.800 --> 00:16:52.330
But secondly, we see lots of pictures throughout
Skidoo World.

00:16:52.330 --> 00:16:53.540
These aren't random photos either.

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:56.389
They all represent different skidoo locations
throughout the series.

00:16:56.389 --> 00:17:00.269
The Planet Picture represents Season two Episode
four - What Experiment Does Blue Want to Try

00:17:00.269 --> 00:17:01.750
where they skidoo into space.

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:06.140
A jungle is Season two Episode four of the
Reboot - Blue's Big Baking Show, where they

00:17:06.140 --> 00:17:09.940
skidoo Into a Jungle and the Gingerbread House
is from season two Episode six of the reboot

00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:13.179
- Blues Night Before Christmas, where they
skidoo to the North Pole.

00:17:13.179 --> 00:17:17.251
These aren't just random places; this world
holds all the places that Josh and Blue have

00:17:17.251 --> 00:17:21.040
been traveling to, and it holds the magic
that makes everything come alive.

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:22.510
This isn't just a portal.

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:23.539
It's a hub world.

00:17:23.539 --> 00:17:27.770
When any of the puppies skidoo, the power
to go there again is stored here in this Skidoo

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:32.200
World, they're capturing different locations
across the world, allowing them to have simultaneous

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:34.210
control over everything.

00:17:34.210 --> 00:17:38.300
Blue and Rainbow Puppy may seem friendly,
but believe me when I say anyone that claims

00:17:38.300 --> 00:17:43.000
to be a dog but can walk, eat chocolate and
have opposable thumbs is someone that cannot

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.040
be trusted.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:47.730
Get as far away as he can from Blue and her
friends because she could be skidooing to

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:49.260
a place near you.

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:51.990
And never, ever go into Blue's room alone.

00:17:51.990 --> 00:17:53.490
They're all just using you.

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:56.870
Instead, you probably just say: So long, there's
no time for one more song.

00:17:56.870 --> 00:18:00.190
If you manage to do that my friends, I got
to thank you for doing your part, you guys

00:18:00.190 --> 00:18:01.580
sure are smart.

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:04.100
but hey, that's just a theory.

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.540
A FILM THEORY!

